From e9e96de73691bf82ae3a2b72b0ad06f9b7a4bf1c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Qi Yu <yuq3@hpc.nih.gov>
Date: Tue, 19 May 2026 16:05:53 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] patch ucsc.R Updated R/ucsc.R:249 to bypass the broken
 restfulr/RCurl UCSC JSON path. The fix adds ucscJSONQuery() and routes
 tableExists, tableNames, ucscSchema, getTable, and ucscGenomes through httr
 instead. I also normalized integer JSON columns in R/ucsc.R:524 back to
 numeric so the existing UCSC tests keep their exact historical behavior.

Verification passed: R CMD INSTALL -l /tmp/rtracklayer-lib .
succeeded, and rtracklayer:::.test() completed with 11 test
functions, 0 errors, 0 failures. The suite still reports 14
warnings, mostly the existing readGFF rewinding warnings, but
the UCSC failures are gone.
---
 R/ucsc.R | 71 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-----------------
 1 file changed, 50 insertions(+), 21 deletions(-)

